    "applicabilityBasis": {
      "summary": "KESm is marketed for remittances and mobile payments and is explicitly classified as reserve-backed in the protocol configuration. MGP-18 identifies its legacy USDm/KESm Broker pool and describes holder exit into USDm, rather than fiat redemption by a named legal issuer. GENIUS sections 2(17) and 2(22) require an issuer obligation to convert, redeem or repurchase for a fixed amount of national currency or a national-currency deposit. A digital asset denominated in a fixed amount of monetary value does not satisfy that redemption limb. The reviewed materials do not establish a person with that statutory conversion, redemption or repurchase obligation. Payment use plus the documented USDm exit makes applicability genuinely ambiguous rather than categorically excluded.",
