    "notes": "KESm remains a legacy shared-reserve FX token, not a USDm-collateralized borrower CDP. MGP-18 explicitly lists KESm among the ten retained V2 FX assets and describes the Broker exit into USDm. Mento Protocol identifies the protocol family, not an established legal issuer or fixed-monetary-value redemption obligor. Mento Labs GmbH is described as an operating and infrastructure provider; Mento Protocol Foundation and AP Reserve Foundation have governance or stewardship roles in MGP-19. Those roles do not establish this token's legal issuer, domicile or GENIUS route, so issuerEntity and issuerDomicile are omitted. MGP-19 is a proposal, not proof of executed control transfers. The public dashboard is reserve or collateral disclosure only. Separate fiat-redemption-policy and monthly-attestation flags are omitted because the reviewed record does not support those findings at high confidence. No U.S. authorization, pending application or registered foreign exception was located in the bounded sources checked. This is not a determination of illegality or an exhaustive review of confidential filings or all state registers.",
